    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102821" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τειχομᾰχ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fight the walls</i>, i.e. <i>conduct siege
				operations</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.70
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.79
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				1.1.14
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					481
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τοὺς πολεμίους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					28
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τειχομαχεῖν δυνατοί</span>
			skilled <i>in conducting sieges</i>, i.e. good engineers, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.102
			</span></i>: perh. of <i>defending a wall</i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Hann.</u>
				92
			</span></i>.</div>
